+// SDL2 host backend, for Linux and Android (and anywhere else SDL2 is), drawing with Vulkan or
+// OpenGL ES 3.0 (gpu.hpp). It follows the Direct3D 11 backend: the GE emits geometry batches
+// already transformed to clip space, which are drawn into one render target per PSP framebuffer
+// address, and the displayed framebuffer is scaled into the window.
+//
+// Environment variables (all optional):
+//   REFRACT_EXIT_AFTER_FRAMES=N   quit after N presented frames
+//   REFRACT_SCREENSHOT_DIR=DIR    save the window as DIR/frame_NNNNNN.ppm ...
+//   REFRACT_SCREENSHOT_EVERY=N    ... every Nth presented frame (default 60)
+//   REFRACT_INPUT_SCRIPT=SCRIPT   scripted button presses "FRAME:MASK[:LENGTH],..."
+//                                 (MASK in hex PSP button bits: START=8, CROSS=4000; bits 28
+//                                 to 31 push the analog stick up, right, down and left, bits
+//                                 24 to 27 the right stick)
+//
+// Keyboard: arrows = d-pad, WASD = analog stick, K/L/J/I = cross/circle/square/triangle,
+// Q/E = L/R, Enter = start, right shift = select. Game controllers use their standard
+// layout.
